espeak-ng 1.52.0 for WebAssembly (text -> IPA phonemes)
=========================================================

This package contains a WebAssembly build of eSpeak NG and data files
compiled from eSpeak NG sources:

  eSpeak NG 1.52.0
  https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
  tag 1.52.0, commit 4870adfa25b1a32b4361592f1be8a40337c58d6c
  source archive https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng/archive/refs/tags/1.52.0.tar.gz
  SHA-256 bb4338102ff3b49a81423da8a1a158b420124b055b60fa76cfb4b18677130a23

  Copyright (C) 2005 to 2013 by Jonathan Duddington
  Copyright (C) 2013-2018 Reece H. Dunn and the eSpeak NG contributors
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your
  option) any later version. The full licence text is in COPYING.

  The bundled ucd-tools library (src/ucd-tools, Copyright (C) 2012-2018
  Reece H. Dunn, GPL-3.0-or-later) is part of the eSpeak NG source tree.
  It contains data derived from the Unicode Character Database, see
  COPYING.UCD in the eSpeak NG source archive.

The data archives contain files compiled from the eSpeak NG 1.52.0 sources
(dictsource/, phsource/, espeak-ng-data/lang/) with a native build of the same
sources; bn_dict and ko_dict are taken from the Homebrew espeak-ng 1.52.0
installation (pinned by SHA-256 in build.sh) because their compilation is not
reproducible.

The espeak-ng sources are used unmodified. Additional files of this package
(conduit_glue.c, conduit_ctype.c, conduit_ctype_override.h,
conduit_ctype_tables.h, index.mjs, phonemizer-compat.mjs, build.sh and the
tools/ and test/ scripts) are a work based on eSpeak NG and are likewise
licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later. phonemizer-compat.mjs re-implements
behaviour of the Python package "phonemizer" (Copyright 2015-2021 Mathieu
Bernard, GPL-3.0-or-later).

The JavaScript runtime glue in espeak-ng.mjs is generated by Emscripten
(MIT / University of Illinois NCSA licence) and contains musl libc
(MIT licence) compiled into espeak-ng.wasm.

Corresponding source: build.sh fetches the exact eSpeak NG source pinned
above; all other sources are included in this package's source tree.
